# Netlify redirect rules — see specs/04-trailing-slash-and-legacy-redirects.md
#
# Syntax: <source> <destination> <status>
# Netlify's CDN normalizes trailing slashes before matching, so each source
# below matches both with and without its trailing slash. Do NOT add rules
# that only add or remove a trailing slash — those loop infinitely.
# Special characters must be percent-encoded on both sides of a rule.

